svg: honor clip-path="url(#id)" referencing a <clipPath>

clip-path was ignored (a TODO in svg_parse_common), so plots from Julia's
Plots.jl and similar, which clip each series to its axes, drew their data
across the neighboring plots (#6544). An element with a clip-path now runs
inside fz_clip_path: the clipPath's shapes are run with svg_draw_path
appending their device-space paths to doc->clip_collect instead of
painting. The clip's user space is the element's, including its own
transform, then the clipPath's transform. The attribute and the style
property are both read. clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox" and text
inside a clipPath are not supported; such elements draw unclipped or
clip to the other shapes.
